      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332535",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the implicit Euler method on the test equation $y^{\u2032} = - \u03bby$ with $y = y(x), y(0) = 1, x \\ge 0, \u03bb = 3$, and step size $\u0394x$?\n\n1. The stability function is $R(3\u0394x) = \\frac{1}{1 + 3\u0394x}$.\n2. The stability region is $\\mid \\frac{1}{1 - 3\u0394x} \\mid < 1$.\n3. The method is absolutely stable.\n4. The method is **unstable** for step size $\u0394x = 0.25$.\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by $y_{n + 1} = R(\u03bb\u0394x)y_{n}$."
    },
