      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-333572",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{\u2032}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=2,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =5,$ and step size $\u0394x?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(5\u0394x)=\\frac{1-5\u0394x/2}{1+5\u0394x/2}.$\n- The stability region is $|\\frac{2-5\u0394x}{2+5\u0394x}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $\u0394x=1.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda \u0394x){y}_{n}.$"
    },
