      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-333574",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{\u2032}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =2,$ and step size $\u0394x?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(2\u0394x)=\\frac{1-\u0394x}{1+\u0394x}.$\n- The stability region is $|2{(\u0394x-1)}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $\u0394x=2.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda \u0394x){y}_{n}.$"
