      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-333930",
      ":question/problem": "For the initial value problem ${y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot \u0394x, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+\u0394{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot \u0394x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{\u2032}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =4,$ and step size $\u0394x?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(4\u0394x)=1-4\u0394x+8(\u0394x)^{2}.$\n- The stability region is $|8{(\u0394x-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is stable for step size $\u0394x=0.5.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda \u0394x){y}_{n}.$"
    },
